 lost their lives to  gun violence and the inaction of our  nation's leaders  one day you will no longer be eight  you'll have a life to sort out you'll  have to decide what kind of person you  want to be despite the pain you carry  you will also have to use wisdom in  choosing The Company You Keep but  throughout your young life you will have  the blessing of good friends friends who  will be there for you and the tough  times  as an 18 year old you still won't know  where life is going to take you  but you should always remember that you  have a community your friends your  family your God and your sister still  sitting next to you on the piano bench  one day you'll sit where I am waiting to  hear from colleges you will be a Sandy  Hook Survivor but you will also be a  regular kid  you will be more than ready to start  your adult life and meet new friends you  will tell them when it's right about the  sister who sang along when you play the  piano  [Music]  oh man that was powerful what a gift  that he has given us I'm you know I've  gotten to know this family very well and  he has turned out to be such an amazing  young man number one the way he wrote  about his sister she loved sharks Lego  and God and what he said about his  parents too Jimmy and Melba that they  will get up even when they don't even  when they don't want to it's so wise  yeah and the honesty about the pain of  what he's been through and when he meets  new people not always saying he has yeah  I never thought about that before Tony  because it opens things up yeah and him  saying he'll decide when he wants to let  people in and he just wrote something  very beautiful to do so and I want to  repeat that because it was powerful he  said you will take comfort in knowing  that even when your parents don't want  to get up they will get up for you I  wrote that too that is heavy he said I'm  a Sandy Hook Survivor but my life is so  much more than that thank you for that  Isaiah please note to self do